\" cy=\"99.25\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(46%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Amsterdam the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.23) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (-0.03).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>54%</td><td class='num'>-0.031</td><td class='num'>21.6%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>42%</td><td class='num'>0.161</td><td class='num'>14.6%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>60%</td><td class='num'>0.223</td><td class='num'>14.5%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>198</td><td class='num'>29%</td><td class='num'>0.234</td><td class='num'>13.6%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":52.37403,"lon":4.88969,"n":737,"n_cities":134,"name":"Amsterdam","offset_days":1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.04,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0032258064516129037,"n":217,"obs":0.12903225806451613,"sig":true},{"hi":0.18,"lo":0.04,"mean":0.09466666666666668,"n":75,"obs":0.30666666666666664,"sig":true},{"hi":0.47,"lo":0.18,"mean":